                <pb facs="0523" n="419" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg419"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/8: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-23T12:00:00+08:00">February 23,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received February 23—2:29 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>262. Following from American Consul General, Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“February 22, 10 a.m. Referring to my despatch of December 20. According
                            to confidential information received by my French colleague, a meeting
                            of Japanese officials and military was held here early last week at
                            which the military proposal to establish a monarchy forthwith with Pu Yi
                            as Emperor was adopted but that instructions were received from Tokyo on
                            the 17th counselling delay. It is now planned according to the same
                            information to inaugurate the new state as a republic by the end of the
                            month with Pu as President and later change it into a
                        monarchy.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
